//// The `onze-cli` package — module-tree root.
////
//// The command line — `create`, `dev`, `build`, `start`, `info` — in
//// `compiler-cli`'s shape (a `main.bp` dispatch, one file per command, pure
//// option parsers). commonJS only: it runs before any BEAM node exists.
////
//// A skeleton created by front 95 (`specs/1.0.10-beta/06-onze/modules.md`
//// § The cut): an empty `pub` surface and one inline test, so the member is a
//// row of `zig build test-libs` from the first commit. Owner: front 50.

test "onze-cli: the member compiles and runs on its rows" {
    assert "onze-cli".length() == 8;
}
